    "result_text": "All 64 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and consolidated duplicate detection onto it, in two files.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `identityKeyFor(...)` now returns the 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously a plain `tel|email|householdId` string). Added standard American **Soundex** (`soundex`/`soundexCode`) and a full-hex `sha256Hex` helper.\n- `rejectDuplicateIdentity(...)` now computes the candidate's full identity key and rejects (409) only when it equals a non-deleted existing owner's key. The separate telephone/email/household 409 blocks are gone \u2014 duplicate detection is the single key. The email-domain block list still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`, before this check).\n- `findPossibleDuplicateOf(...)` now flags a **soft match** when `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match but the identity key differs (it takes the normalized email so it can compute the key). It picks the lowest existing id.\n- Removed the now-unused `DuplicateEmailException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` imports and the household-duplicate throw.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- The `identityKey` response field is now derived via `deriveIdentityKey(owner)`, using the same Soundex + SHA-256 logic so the returned key matches what duplicate detection compares. The Soundex/hash helpers are `private static` so MapStruct doesn't treat them as `String\u2192String` mapping candidates.\n\nBehavioural effects, matching the spec and the updated tests:\n- Two owners with the same lastName + postcode but different telephones are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they're created and the second is flagged `possibleDuplicate` (Cp10, Cp35).\n- A full identity repeat (same telephone/email/lastName) still collides with 409 (Cp03, Cp25, Cp28, Cp52).\n- `householdId`, household member counts, and membership scoring are unchanged (Cp11, Cp23, Cp36, Cp39 still green).",
